            <ArticleTitle>[Diagnostic significance of phase transition temperatures of blood serum cholesterol in atherosclerosis].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>92-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Lipid parameters and temperatures of serum cholesterol; ethers phasic transition were investigated in 35 patients with atherosclerosis of lower-limb vessels, 93 patients with atherosclerosis of coronary arteries and 40 normal subjects. The correlation between transition temperatures and the fatty-acid spectrum of cholesterol ether fraction was examined. Temperatures of cholesterol ethers phasic transition are suggested as diagnostic criteria to supplement conventional biochemical tests.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
